A function that is stored in a record updates the record that its receiver hands it (ownership-v2.md §2.1, The row of a record; §2.11.5, the record pass; #2477): `g = λs → { s | b = s.b }`, applied by `app` to the new literal `lit`. Checker v1 holds that update pending, because the function is stored in a record. Checker v2 accepts it at the call of `app` (`callback-param`). Built again under --ownership=v2 --records-in-place, with the stale-read sanitiser, with the stores as they ship, and as a release: each build prints the golden.
